id: pm-mav1ak
title: "Uniform row-streaming contract: every row-producing read emits incremental line-delimited rows in constant memory"
description: "Converge --stream and --format ndjson onto one contract-declared streaming mode available on every row-producing read surface, backed by a real incremental producer with a bounded-memory gate, a self-describing trailer record, and correct early-termination behaviour."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",composability,scale
created_at: "2026-07-25T17:49:14.861Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T08:52:35.848Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#52e09ad611fe4b76c9f77dec"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "Every row-producing read (list, search, context, next, activity, graph, aggregate, deps) supports line-delimited row output through one contract-declared mode with both existing spellings preserved as aliases; rows are produced incrementally through an SDK iterator path, proven by a bounded-heap test over a large synthetic workspace and an early-termination test asserting the producer stops when the consumer closes the pipe; envelope metadata (count, cursor, truncation) is emitted as a final trailer record carrying a declared discriminator key so streams stay self-describing and resumable via --after; EPIPE is handled silently with the exit code declared by the pm-psy1 scripting contract; the row schema per surface is contract-declared and drift-gated; docs carry worked jq and xargs pipelines against a million-item workspace"
parent: pm-9rxu
risk: medium
confidence: high
