comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T07:36:48.392Z","harness:codex","Progress evidence 2026-08-17: introduced the shared pm.stream.trailer serializer, applied it to resumable mutation-event batches and idle heartbeats, and proved clean installed-exporter artifact channels. Linked exemplar tests passed 23/23 and the repository remains exact 100/100/100/100. This is substantive progress, but the feature remains open because list, search, context, next, activity, graph, aggregate, and deps still need convergence on one incremental constant-memory iterator contract with EPIPE and million-item gates."
  "2026-08-17T08:52:35.848Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review remediation completed across all ten CodeRabbit findings: initial-page consumption is documented; exporter authoring types and blueprint options align; trailer input is explicit; reserved rows and discriminator overrides are rejected; invalid CLI/runtime cursor values fail closed; compatibility iteration forces row mode; generated descriptions match; and artifact outputs reject ambiguous ownership/unknown fields. The expanded Bun recurrence pm-b8hwfr is also implemented after manual packed acceptance. Exact full coverage passes 512 files / 7,469 tests at 100/100/100/100."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T07:36:49.270Z","harness:codex","A discriminator-bearing terminal record can preserve counts, cursors, truncation, and provenance without forcing row buffering. Batch boundaries and exporter channel ownership are reusable primitives, but the parent must remain open until every enumerated row-producing surface adopts the same producer and early-termination contract."
